Yes, 14 Mill Wynd is in the **Glenarrow Town Centre conservation area**. It is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

Under the council's windows guidance, replacing windows in a conservation area needs a planning application unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So if you want to change the material (for example, timber to uPVC) or the glazing pattern or style, you will likely need to apply. If the replacements are an exact match, you may not need one, but I can't give a formal opinion on that. I'd suggest contacting the planning desk to confirm before you start work.
